        "target": "First, I identify the given quantities:\n- John's old apartment cost: $1200 per month\n- New apartment cost: 40% more than $1200\n- Number of people splitting the new apartment: 3 (John and his two brothers)\n\nTo find the cost of the new apartment, I calculate 40% of $1200 and add it to $1200:\n\\[ 1200 \\times 0.40 = 480 \\]\n\\[ 1200 + 480 = 1680 \\]\n\nThis is the total monthly cost of the new apartment. To find the cost per person, I divide by 3:\n\\[ 1680 \\div 3 = 560 \\]\n\nSo, each person pays $560 per month for the new apartment. Now, I calculate the annual cost for both the old and new apartments:\n- Old apartment annual cost: \\( 1200 \\times 12 = 14400 \\)\n- New apartment annual cost: \\( 560 \\times 12 = 6720 \\)\n\nTo find the annual savings, I subtract the new apartment's annual cost from the old apartment's annual cost:\n\\[ 14400 - 6720 = 7680 \\]\n\nFINAL: 7680",
