        "student_prefix_sha256": "f5182542566756ec731bead317148c66cde3de50dafdaa62db75e91db910016d",
        "target": "First, I identify the given quantities:\n- Adam earns $40 daily.\n- 10% of his earnings are deducted as taxes.\n- He works for 30 days.\n\nThe unknown is:\n- How much money Adam will have earned after taxes after 30 days.\n\nTo solve this, I'll follow these steps:\n1. Calculate the daily earnings after taxes.\n2. Multiply the daily after-tax earnings by the number of days worked.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the daily earnings after taxes.\n- 10% of $40 is $40 * 0.10 = $4.\n- So, the daily earnings after taxes are $40 - $4 = $36.\n\nStep 2: Calculate the total earnings after taxes for 30 days.\n- $36 per day * 30 days = $1080.\n\nTherefore, Adam will have earned $1080 after taxes after 30 days of work.\n\nFINAL: 1080",
